# support_triage

A second business domain on the same [`business_agent`](../business_agent) core.

It exists to answer one question honestly: *is the core actually reusable, or is
it a WeChat agent with the serial numbers filed off?*

So it shares nothing with the order domain except the core:

| | order_agent | support_triage |
| --- | --- | --- |
| input | a customer order message | any inbound support message |
| output | intent + items + evidence | category + urgency + reply suggestion |
| policy | record automatically? | escalate or answer? |

It imports no WeChat, no Windows automation, no order database, no product login
and no billing module.

## Run

```bash
pip install -e packages/support_triage
support-triage --text "我要退款"

# or without installing
PYTHONPATH=packages/business_agent/src:packages/support_triage/src \
  python -m support_triage --text "我的订单还没到" --json
```

```text
输入：我要退款
状态：needs_review（需要您确认）
分类：refund　紧急度：urgent
回复建议：已收到您的退款诉求，正在为您核实。
  · 需要关注：needs_human — routed to a human by policy
```

## Policy

A refund dispute is never auto-answered, no matter how confident a model sounds.
Neither is an ungrounded citation: if the evidence quote does not appear in the
message, the result is escalated rather than applied.

## Swapping in a real model

The default backend is deterministic so the example runs with no credentials.
For a real run:

```python
from business_agent import AgentCore, ModelApiBackend
from support_triage import SupportTriagePlugin, triage

backend = ModelApiBackend(base_url=..., api_key=..., model=...)
result = triage("我的订单还没到", backend=backend)
result.usage.model_executed   # True
```
